---
import Layout from '../../layouts/default.astro';

---
<Layout title="Service Terms | MECS" description="Service terms and conditions for ME Computer Services.">
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Service Terms</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Practical IT help. Clear fixed prices.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-content">
      <h2>Service Terms and Conditions</h2>
      <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> [Effective Date]</p>
      
      <p>These terms and conditions govern the provision of services by ME Computer Services (MECS). By engaging our services, you agree to these terms.</p>
      
      <h3>Scope of Services</h3>
      <p>MECS provides IT services as described in our service offerings. The specific scope of work for each engagement will be detailed in a written agreement or service order.</p>
      
      <h3>Pricing and Payment</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>All prices are fixed and quoted in advance.</li>
        <li>Payment is due upon completion of services unless otherwise agreed.</li>
        <li>Accepted payment methods: [Accepted payment methods]</li>
        <li>Late payments may incur interest charges at [Interest rate]% per month.</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h3>Client Responsibilities</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide access to necessary equipment and systems.</li>
        <li>Ensure that data is backed up before service begins (we recommend but do not perform backups unless explicitly included in the scope).</li>
        <li>Designate a point of contact for communication.</li>
        <li>Inform us of any relevant security or compliance requirements.</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h3>Warranty and Liability</h3>
      <p>MECS warrants that services will be performed in a professional and workmanlike manner. Our liability is limited to the amount paid for the specific service that gave rise to the claim.</p>
      
      <h3>Confidentiality</h3>
      <p>We will treat all client information as confidential and will not disclose it to third parties without your consent, except as required by law.</p>
      
      <h3>Termination</h3>
      <p>Either party may terminate the engagement with written notice. Payment for services rendered up to the termination date is due.</p>
      
      <h3>Governing Law</h3>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of [Governing law jurisdiction].</p>
      
      <h3>Changes to Terms</h3>
      <p>MECS reserves the right to update these terms and conditions. Continued use of our services after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>
      
      <!-- TODO: Review and customize these service terms for your specific business needs and consult with a legal professional to ensure compliance with applicable laws. -->
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>